Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Suggested Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0870634f-e2d8-4496-ad22-f265aa04a284"],

Cell["\<\
1. Note in Lab G2A that 2-spin INEPT depends on tau1 + tau2 = 1/(2J); compare \
LBFGS and HybridLBFGSNewtonCG convergence speed and final sum across \
different J values.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d589ea5f-5c42-4420-b5ce-b258c9f719ac"],

Cell["\<\
2. In Lab G2B, increase Static Events from 4 to 80 and watch Fused Stages \
remain constant (4) while the fusion speedup grows steadily.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d8ac1f86-2617-4d3f-9d92-263af6490ae8"],

Cell["\<\
3. Notice that bounded 2nd-order solvers require BoundTransform -> \
\"Sigmoid\" or \"Log\" (passing BoundTransform -> \"None\" cleanly emits \
OptimalControlProblem::unconstronly).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f4887bec-8e6c-4521-9ea0-27ed02890826"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1f04b123-c300-4338-8e70-b25c85860b5e"],

Cell["\<\
Automatic coordinate scaling, exact O(K) Hilbert HVPs, smooth Sigmoid/Log \
bound transforms, and compile-time static fusion deliver rapid \
quadratic/superlinear convergence on multi-scale constrained NMR problems.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"077ea55e-63de-4fc1-a1fd-b5303e71793e"],

